    "explanation": "The arithmetic decides this case, and both sides largely agree on the facts. EV-TRIP-00503, EV-GPS-00503 and EV-FARE-00503 all carry trip TRP-00503 and match on the pickup timestamp, so they describe the same trip. Under POL-RD-01 the governing measurement is gps_trace.trace_distance_km = 6.81 km against the booked optimal of 4.2 km, an excess of 2.61 km or 62.14% - clearing both establishment gates (more than 0.8 km and more than 20%) and landing in the material band above 50%. The trace is unimpaired: 175 fixes at a 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, a maximum gap of 0.0 seconds and no gaps, so POL-RD-07 does not engage and no corroboration is required.\n\nThe remedy is arithmetic under POL-RD-02. The fare model on EV-FARE-00503 is METERED, so POL-RD-11 does not apply. recomputed_fare = (3.80 base fare + 0.75 x 4.2 optimal km + 0.28 x 7.5 optimal min) x the surge_multiplier read from the fare breakdown (1.0) = 9.05, plus the 0.80 platform fee = 9.85. Refund = charged_total 17.82 - 9.85 = 7.97, rounded UP to 8.00. That is 44.9% of the charge: above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor, so NO_ACTION is not available, and below the 90% share, so FULL_REFUND is not available. The outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 8.00.\n\nTo the driver: 'the navigation chose the road' is not a defence in this policy. POL-RD-01 measures the deviation on the trace, not on fault, and POL-RD-08 puts the burden on you to name a specific artifact and clause for any exoneration. None is available: the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00503-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 (issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT), so no closure can be run under POL-RD-03; EV-CHAT-00503 holds zero messages, so POL-RD-04 finds no rider instruction; EV-TRIP-00503 shows no pickup/dropoff amendment and a null amended_optimal_distance_km, so POL-RD-05 does not run; and the vehicle is RYDE_X with solo_optimal_distance_km null, so POL-RD-12 does not apply. Your statement that the route looked odd does not change the result - the deviation is already established on a clean trace.\n\nTo the rider: the missed lesson and the 'almost double' fare are not compensable heads under this policy; the refund is the arithmetical figure above. No pass-through correction arises - erp_gantries is empty, tolls, off-route ERP and airport surcharge are all 0.00, and the billed 6.8 km matches the trace 6.81 km - so POL-RD-09 adds nothing, creates no billing-integrity referral, and no driver compensation is owed (shortfall 0.01 km). Because the deviation is material, POL-RD-06 required the driver-profile check: deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 250 completed trips, so no pattern is established, no FULL_REFUND uplift applies and no driver-conduct referral arises. The absent advisory neither helps nor hurts the money; a MISSING artifact at weight 0.0 can carry no fact, and the deciding facts here rest on artifacts at weight 1.0, so confidence is 0.9."
